    15	# Design analysis for the D1 inversion variant
    16	# --------------------------------------------
    17	# a) Concrete behavior trace
    18	# - The input still contains two large non-black regions on a black background,
    19	#   with black dents and one-cell noise. The solver still has to clean the
    20	#   regions first, then identify every original black cell whose cleaned 3x3
    21	#   neighborhood clearly belongs to one host color.
    22	# - Original behavior at one dent:
    23	#     clean 3x3 majority = red -> paint the whole 3x3 yellow -> recolor center teal.
    24	# - Variant behavior at the same dent:
    25	#     clean 3x3 majority = red -> paint the whole 3x3 red -> recolor center teal.
    26	# - The difference matters most when the 3x3 touches background or the other
    27	#   region. In that case the original task "plants" a foreign-color block,
    28	#   while the variant "repairs" the host region by expanding its own color into
    29	#   nearby non-host cells. Interior dents remain mostly teal-center markers.
    30	#
    31	# b) Complexity calibration
    32	# - If dents were mostly deep inside solid rectangles, the new 3x3 repaint would
    33	#   often be visually indistinguishable from simply restoring the center before
    34	#   marking it teal. That would weaken the D1 signal.
    35	# - To keep the variant observable without changing the task family, the
    36	#   generator requires visible edge-adjacent dents for both foreground colors,
    37	#   while still keeping many interior dents. This preserves repeated evidence
    38	#   for "same-side repair" in 2-4 ARC examples without over-constraining layout
    39	#   sampling.
    40	#
    41	# c) Main() line-by-line assumption review
    42	# - _main_colors assumes exactly two dominant foreground colors after excluding
    43	#   black; that still holds because the input palette is unchanged.
    44	# - _clean_foreground assumes all non-main colors are noise and should collapse
    45	#   to black or the local majority. That remains valid because the variant only
    46	#   changes the final dent repaint, not the corruption model.
    47	# - _dent_centers assumes a dent can be assigned to the local majority color if
    48	#   that color has at least 5 cells in the cleaned 3x3 and strictly beats the
    49	#   other color. This still defines the host region correctly for the variant.
    50	# - The original main() relied on the extra step "host -> other" when stamping
    51	#   the 3x3 patch. That is the only old-property dependency that must change.
    52	#   In the variant, stamping must use host directly; otherwise the solver would
    53	#   silently revert to the old rule.
    54	#
    55	# d) Placement legality
    56	# - Dent centers are only chosen from host-colored cells whose 3x3 neighborhood
    57	#   still has at least 5 host cells after removing the center. This guarantees
    58	#   the solver can recover the host color from the input.
    59	# - Centers keep Chebyshev distance >= 3 from other chosen centers of the same
    60	#   color, preventing accidental overlap between unrelated 3x3 patches.
    61	# - Optional 2-cell dents are added only when the second cell is also a valid
    62	#   dent center and does not crowd other same-color dents.
    63	#
    64	# e) Visual observability
    65	# - The generator classifies dent candidates as "visible-patch" when their
    66	#   clean 3x3 already contains at least one non-host cell. These are the cases
    67	#   where same-color stamping visibly extends the region.
    68	# - Each generated grid must contain at least one such dent per foreground
    69	#   color, and usually more. This avoids a degenerate dataset where the variant
    70	#   is technically correct but hard to infer by eye.
    71	#
    72	# f) Visual cleanliness
    73	# - Noise remains one-cell only, and dents are spaced apart. The output shows
    74	#   large clean regions plus teal markers, with only local 3x3 repairs around
    75	#   dents. That keeps the image readable even when some repairs clip over region
    76	#   boundaries or into background.
    77	#
    78	# g) Color inference
    79	# - No hidden color ordering is introduced. The host color comes purely from the
    80	#   visible majority in the cleaned 3x3. The only special output color remains
    81	#   teal at dent centers, matching the original task family.
    82	#
    83	# h) New implicit assumptions after the change
    84	# - main() now assumes that at least some dents have non-host cells in their
